{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Coarse meal, fine flour.</b> Fine flour (סֹלֶת) for cakes; coarse meal (קֶמַח) for the cooks' thickening, to cover the pot and draw off the scum — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 18:6). And so it is in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 48:12), and there they explained that there were three se'ah for each one. And we do not know why he made so much bread for three men — perhaps he knew that each dish would be withdrawn as soon as it was served, and so he was like one who offers many sacrifices upon the altar, or perhaps the great ones of his household dined with them in their honor. And according to the plain sense: 'Make haste, three se'ah of coarse meal, to make fine flour from it' — and behold, she produced from all the three se'ah only a little fine flour."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:52.608219586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}